+# Aspose.HTML FOSS for Python
+
+![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.10%2B-blue.svg)
+
+Aspose.HTML FOSS for Python reads HTML input and parses it into a standards-based DOM tree using `HTMLDocument.parse`, `HTMLDocument.parse_fragment`, and `tree.parse_html`. It writes serialized markup output using serialise and `XMLSerializer`. It applies `CSS` by attaching `CSSStyleSheet` objects and resolving computed styles via `ComputedStyleDeclaration`, supports `CSS` selector matching with `aspose_html.css.select`, and detects byte-stream encoding with `detect_encoding`. It handles `URL` parsing and query parameter manipulation with `URL` and `URLSearchParams`, and provides optional JavaScript execution through `JSContext` backed by QuickJS.
+
+Aspose.HTML FOSS for Python is a free, open-source, MIT-licensed Python toolkit for parsing HTML into a standards-based DOM tree, applying CSS, and serializing markup back out. It provides WHATWG-style `HTMLDocument`/`Document`/`Element` APIs, CSS selector matching and CSSOM-based computed-style resolution, WHATWG `URL`/`URLSearchParams` handling, and byte-stream encoding detection, with an optional QuickJS-backed JavaScript execution bridge for running scripts against the parsed DOM.
