+## Key Capabilities
+
+- **Parse HTML into DOM.** It parses HTML strings, bytes, fragments, and files into a DOM document using `aspose_html.HTMLDocument.parse`, `aspose_html.HTMLDocument.parse_fragment`, and `aspose_html.HTMLDocument.load`, while `aspose_html.tree.parse_html` and `aspose_html.tree.TreeBuilder` provide lower-level control over the tokenization and tree-construction process.
+- **DOM manipulation and querying.** It builds, inspects, and mutates DOM trees by creating and updating nodes programmatically with `aspose_html.dom.Document.create_element` and `append_child`, reading and writing element attributes, classes, datasets, inline styles, and text content, and querying documents by ID, tag name, class name, and selector-oriented helpers such as `get_element_by_id`, `get_elements_by_tag_name`, `TreeWalker`, `NodeIterator`, and `Range`.
+- **CSSOM styling and computed styles.** It matches `CSS` selectors and stylesheets against elements and resolves the cascade—including specificity, inline-vs-author rules, !important, and inheritance—with `aspose_html.dom.Element.get_computed_style`, while the CSSOM surface provided by `aspose_html.cssom.CSSStyleSheet`, `aspose_html.cssom.CSSStyleRule`, `aspose_html.cssom.CSSMediaRule`, and `aspose_html.dom.ComputedStyleDeclaration` models stylesheets structurally.
+- **URL and encoding utilities.** It validates and manipulates URLs with `aspose_html.url.URL`, reads and edits query strings with `aspose_html.url.URLSearchParams`, and detects byte-stream character encodings using BOM and content sniffing with `aspose_html.encoding.detect_encoding`.
+- **JavaScript execution bridge.** It executes JavaScript against a parsed DOM through `aspose_html.js.JSContext`, an optional QuickJS-backed bridge exposing DOM read-only proxies to script code, requiring the js extra dependency quickjs>=1.19,<2.
+- **Low-level parsing control.** It implements the WHATWG tokenization and tree-construction algorithms directly through `aspose_html.tokenizer.Tokenizer` and `aspose_html.tokenizer.StartTagToken`, enabling callers who need low-level control over the parsing process.
+- **HTML element specialization.** It exposes specialized HTML element classes such as `aspose_html.dom.HTMLInputElement`, `aspose_html.dom.HTMLTableElement`, and `aspose_html.dom.HTMLMediaElement`, each providing element-specific properties defined by their HTML interface.
+- **Serialization to markup.** It serializes complete documents, fragments, and individual elements back to an HTML string using `aspose_html.serialise` or `aspose_html.XMLSerializer`, with `aspose_html.serialiser.outer_html` providing additional control over the output format.
